1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,043
Previously on Friends...

2
00:00:02,085 --> 00:00:03,629
Erica, are... are you okay?

3
00:00:03,671 --> 00:00:05,547
Yeah. You know,
maybe I ate too much.

4
00:00:05,589 --> 00:00:07,299
I keep getting
these stomachaches.

5
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:09,468
They come and go,
like, every few minutes.

6
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,262
Oh, my God!

7
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:15,975
Relax. We'll just
get her some antacids.

8
00:00:16,015 --> 00:00:17,476
She doesn't have a stomachache!

9
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:18,686
She's in labor!

10
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:19,770
Oh, my God!

11
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:21,104
So if you think

12
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,397
that I didn't
say good-bye to you

13
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,941
because you don't
mean as much to me

14
00:00:23,983 --> 00:00:25,693
as everybody else,
you're wrong.

15
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:27,486
It's because you
mean more to me.

16
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:28,696
Rach!

17
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:29,613
What?

18
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:54,013
Hey.

19
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:57,516
Shh! Go back to sleep.

20
00:00:57,558 --> 00:00:59,685
I have to go home.

21
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:00,936
Oh, God.

22
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:02,437
This was amazing.

23
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:04,815
It really was.

24
00:01:05,983 --> 00:01:08,527
You've learned
some new moves.

25
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:10,946
Yeah, well, this guy at work

26
00:01:10,988 --> 00:01:13,949
gave me Sex For Dummies
as a joke.

27
00:01:13,991 --> 00:01:15,534
Who's laughing now?

28
00:01:15,576 --> 00:01:16,577
I know.

29
00:01:23,834 --> 00:01:28,338
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

30
00:01:28,380 --> 00:01:30,549
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

31
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:34,177
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:38,223
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

33
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:40,392
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

34
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,728
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

35
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:46,565
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

36
00:01:46,607 --> 00:01:49,109
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

37
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,653
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

38
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:54,364
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

39
00:01:54,406 --> 00:01:57,076
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

40
00:01:57,116 --> 00:02:02,497
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

41
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:11,673
Okay, breathe.
breathe, breathe.

42
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:13,383
Oh!

43
00:02:13,425 --> 00:02:14,635
Okay, good.

44
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,386
Next time,
can I say breathe?

45
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:19,514
No. Last time, you said it like
Dracula, and it scared her.

46
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,224
Can I get
you anything?

47
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,310
You want some more ice chips?

48
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:25,020
No. I'm okay.

49
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:27,689
All right,
I'll be right back.

50
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:29,483
Where you going?

51
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:31,150
To use the bathroom.

52
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:33,028
You can't leave me
alone with her.

53
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,738
What?

54
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:37,699
This is exactly the kind
of social situation

55
00:02:37,741 --> 00:02:39,827
that I am not
comfortable with.

56
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:44,123
What kind of social situation
are you comfortable with?

57
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:46,207
It's just that
we've never spent

58
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:48,585
any time, you know,
alone together.

59
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,129
You'll be fine.

60
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:52,798
Nah, you won't, but I'll
be back in two minutes.

61
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,841
Okay.

62
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:05,686
So, uh... any plans
for the summer?

63
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:08,229
I don't know.

64
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:09,773
Maybe church camp.

65
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:14,277
Hah!

66
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:16,321
May not want to mention this.

67
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:21,576
So, you ever wonder
which is worse?

68
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:26,623
You know, going through labor
or getting kicked in the nuts?

69
00:03:26,665 --> 00:03:28,583
What?

70
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,086
Oh, it's just interesting,
you know?

71
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:33,254
Because no one will ever know,

72
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,757
because no one
can experience both.

73
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:42,430
One of life's great
unanswerable questions.

74
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,726
I mean, who knows?

75
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:47,227
Maybe there's something

76
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,104
even more painful
than those things.

77
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,525
Like this.

78
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,490
( knocking )
Come in.

79
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:01,491
Morning.

80
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:02,492
Hey.

81
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:03,994
What's that?

82
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:06,287
It's my housewarming present
for Monica and Chandler.

83
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:07,664
( chirping )

84
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:10,792
Oh! Oh, it's a baby
chick and duck.

85
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:13,879
Uh-huh. And I named them
Chick Jr. and Duck Jr.

86
00:04:13,921 --> 00:04:15,797
I did not
see that coming.

87
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,298
Yeah, yeah.

88
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:19,093
I figured they'd love it
at the new house, you know?

89
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:20,260
It has that big backyard.

90
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,428
And then,
when they get old,

91
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:22,804
they can go
to that special farm

92
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:24,765
that Chandler took
the other chick and duck to.

93
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:28,351
Yes.

94
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,187
You know, it's a shame
people can't visit there.

95
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:31,855
That is
the rule though.

96
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:32,898
Yeah.

97
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:37,069
Guess what!

98
00:04:37,111 --> 00:04:38,570
You're
almost an uncle.

99
00:04:38,612 --> 00:04:39,988
What?
Yeah. Erica went

100
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:41,448
into labor last night;

101
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:42,824
Monica and Chandler
are at the hospital right now.

102
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:43,992
Oh, my God!

103
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:44,910
And I have
a definite feeling

104
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:45,911
it's going to be a girl.

105
00:04:45,953 --> 00:04:47,162
Phoebe, you were sure

106
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:48,705
Ben was going
to be a girl.

107
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,165
Have you seen him
throw a ball?

108
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:55,336
Is Rachel here?

109
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,172
Uh, I think
she's still asleep.

110
00:04:57,214 --> 00:04:58,966
Hey, hey, hey. How
did it go with you
guys last night?

111
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:01,301
She seemed pretty
pissed at you.

112
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:04,805
We, uh... you know,
we worked things out.

113
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,306
What's
that smile?

114
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,558
Did something happen
with you two?

115
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,769
Hey, I'm not one
to kiss and tell.

116
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:13,730
But I'm also not one to have sex
and shut up.

117
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:15,232
We totally did it!

118
00:05:15,274 --> 00:05:16,524
Oh, my God!

119
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:18,318
You and Rachel?

120
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,903
I know. Isn't
this pretty great?

121
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,113
So what does that mean?

122
00:05:21,155 --> 00:05:22,823
Are you guys
getting back together?

123
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:24,324
Oh, I don't know.

124
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,160
I mean, we didn't
really get to talk.

125
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:27,744
But do you want
to get back together?

126
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:29,329
I don't know.

127
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:30,831
It was incredible.

128
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:33,167
I mean, it just felt so right.

129
00:05:33,208 --> 00:05:35,002
When I was holding her,

130
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:38,337
I mean, I... I never
wanted to let her go.

131
00:05:38,379 --> 00:05:40,381
You know what? Yeah, I do.

132
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:42,176
I want to be together.

133
00:05:42,217 --> 00:05:43,010
Yay!

134
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:43,635
Shh!

135
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,344
Yay!

136
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:46,721
Hey, hey, hey.

137
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:49,183
So... so, is she
still going to Paris?

138
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:50,600
Well, I haven't thought of that.

139
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:51,768
I... I hope not.

140
00:05:51,810 --> 00:05:53,687
This is like the
best day ever. Ever!

141
00:05:53,728 --> 00:05:55,438
You guys might
get back together.

142
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,732
Monica and Chandler
are getting their baby.

143
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:01,695
There are chicks and ducks
in the world again. Oh!

144
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,864
I feel like I'm in a musical.

145
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,782
( humming intro )

146
00:06:05,824 --> 00:06:09,744
♪ When the sun comes up
bright and beaming ♪

147
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,705
♪ And the moon
comes... ♪
Morning.

148
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,874
Guess you'll never
know how it ends.

149
00:06:15,167 --> 00:06:16,126
Hey.

150
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:17,127
Hi.

151
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:18,295
How did you sleep?

152
00:06:18,337 --> 00:06:20,047
Good. You?

153
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,215
Good.

154
00:06:21,256 --> 00:06:23,717
I'll bet
you did.

155
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:27,428
Uh... would you guys
mind giving us a minute?

156
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,889
Sure. Yeah.
Will you just
keep an eye

157
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,057
on the chick
and the duck?

158
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,059
Chick and the duck?
Didn't they die?

159
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,643
Dive.

160
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:35,478
Yeah, they dove...

161
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,481
headfirst into
fun on the farm.

162
00:06:45,364 --> 00:06:46,865
So...

163
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,493
Morning.

164
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,913
You, too.

165
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:54,748
Last night was
just wonderful.

166
00:06:54,789 --> 00:06:56,250
It really was.

167
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:57,751
I woke up today

168
00:06:57,792 --> 00:06:59,253
with the biggest smile
on my face.

169
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:00,879
Yeah. Me, too.
It was...

170
00:07:00,921 --> 00:07:03,590
You know, it was, like,
one of those things

171
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:06,927
you think is never going
to happen, and then it does,

172
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,346
and it's everything
you want it to be.

173
00:07:09,388 --> 00:07:10,764
Mm-hmm. I know.

174
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,140
It was just...

175
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:16,770
Oh, just the perfect
way to say good-bye.

176
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,279
( groaning )

177
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,780
Just a little
bit more, honey.

178
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,615
Hell, man,
this hurts!

179
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:30,117
Really? That bad?

180
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,534
Uh-huh. I think it's time

181
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:33,120
to kick you in the nuts
and see which is worse.

182
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:37,874
The baby's head is crowning.

183
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:40,127
Oh, my God!

184
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:43,338
That is the most
beautiful top of a
head I have ever seen.

185
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,132
Chandler, you
have to see this.

186
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:46,674
I'm okay.

187
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:49,970
Chandler, you don't
want to miss this.

188
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:51,471
This is the birth
of your child.

189
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:52,806
It's the miracle
of life.

190
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:54,349
All right.

191
00:07:56,476 --> 00:08:00,272
Wow. That is one
disgusting miracle.

192
00:08:00,314 --> 00:08:02,399
Start pushing.
There you go.

193
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:05,319
Here come
the shoulders.

194
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:10,449
( baby crying )

195
00:08:10,489 --> 00:08:12,951
It's a boy.

196
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:14,161
Wow.

197
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,370
Is he okay?

198
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:17,080
He's just fine.

199
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:18,873
You did it.

200
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,875
It's a baby.

201
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:22,669
A beautiful
little baby.

202
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,296
And some other stuff

203
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:26,840
I'm going to pretend
I don't see.

204
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:30,510
Would you like to
cut the umbilical cord?

205
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:38,977
Well, that's spongy.

206
00:08:39,019 --> 00:08:42,147
Oh...

207
00:08:42,189 --> 00:08:44,774
Hey, handsome.

208
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:46,860
Oh, I'm going
to love you so much

209
00:08:46,901 --> 00:08:49,570
that no woman
is ever going

210
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:52,115
to be good
enough for you.

211
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:53,700
Oh, we're so lucky.

212
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,910
I know.

213
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:57,954
He has your eyes.

214
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:02,042
I mean, I know
that's not possible,

215
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,377
but he does.

216
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:05,628
We'll just get him
cleaned up a bit.

217
00:09:07,005 --> 00:09:09,007
MONICA:
Oh, my God.

218
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:10,717
He's beautiful.

219
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:12,886
Thank you so much.

220
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:15,055
I'm really happy for you guys.

221
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:16,597
How do you feel?

222
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:18,141
I'm tired.

223
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:20,852
You don't have that
much time to relax.

224
00:09:20,894 --> 00:09:22,437
The other one will
be along in a minute.

225
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:29,486
I... I'm sorry?

226
00:09:29,528 --> 00:09:31,988
Who should be along
in a what, now?

227
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:35,534
The next baby should
be along in a minute.

228
00:09:35,574 --> 00:09:39,246
We only ordered one.

229
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:42,374
You know it's twins, right?

230
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:46,878
Oh, yeah. These are
the faces of two
people in the know.

231
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,219
I can't believe you
didn't know it's twins.

232
00:09:54,261 --> 00:09:56,012
This has never happened before.

233
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:59,558
Well, gosh, that
makes me feel so
special and good.

234
00:09:59,598 --> 00:10:01,976
Wait. Did you
know it was twins?

235
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:04,062
Yeah. It's here in the paperwork
we got from the clinic in Ohio.

236
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,813
Did anybody tell you?

237
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,524
I don't think so.

238
00:10:07,566 --> 00:10:09,943
Although they did mention
something about two heartbeats.

239
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:12,153
But I thought that
was just mine and the baby's.

240
00:10:12,195 --> 00:10:14,489
They kept saying both
heartbeats are really strong.

241
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:17,367
And I thought, well, that's
good, 'cause I'm having a baby.

242
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:20,912
This is unbelievable.

243
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,539
Twins actually run in my family.

244
00:10:22,581 --> 00:10:24,082
Interesting.

245
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:27,377
Can I see you
for a second?

246
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:31,256
What do we do?

247
00:10:31,298 --> 00:10:32,591
What do you mean,
what do we do?

248
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,675
Twins.

249
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:36,386
Twins.

250
00:10:36,428 --> 00:10:38,346
Chandler, you're panicking.

251
00:10:38,388 --> 00:10:40,848
Uh-huh.
Join me, won't you?

252
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:42,725
Okay, what do you
say we keep one

253
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:46,187
and then just, like,
have an option
on the other one?

254
00:10:46,229 --> 00:10:48,982
Chandler,
we can't split them up.
Why not?

255
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,401
We could give each
of them half a medallion.

256
00:10:51,443 --> 00:10:54,154
And then, years later,
they'll find each other...

257
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:57,698
and be reunited.

258
00:10:57,740 --> 00:11:00,285
I mean, that's a great
day for everybody.

259
00:11:00,327 --> 00:11:01,786
Okay, what
if the person

260
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:04,372
who adopts the other
one is horrible?

261
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:05,706
What if they're not?

262
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,542
What if it's
adopted by a king?

263
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:10,253
Yeah, because I hear the king
is looking to adopt.

264
00:11:10,295 --> 00:11:14,341
Monica, we're not ready
to have two babies.

265
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,842
That doesn't matter.

266
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:17,594
We have waited
so long for this.

267
00:11:17,636 --> 00:11:19,346
I don't care
if it's two babies.

268
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:21,264
I don't care if
it's three babies.

269
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:23,016
I don't care
if the entire cast

270
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:25,185
of Eight is Enough
comes out of there.

271
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:30,190
We are taking them home
because they are our children.

272
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,691
Okay. Shh!

273
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:35,570
Okay.
Okay!

274
00:11:35,612 --> 00:11:36,779
Okay!

275
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,949
It looks like we're
about ready over here.

276
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:42,910
Come on, Erica,
start pushing again now.

277
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:44,371
Oh! Oh!

278
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:45,497
Here she comes.

279
00:11:45,539 --> 00:11:48,249
She? It's a girl?

280
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:49,250
Yeah.

281
00:11:52,003 --> 00:11:53,505
Well, now we have
one of each!

282
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,258
And that's enough.

283
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:01,095
And then she said it was

284
00:12:01,137 --> 00:12:03,890
the perfect way to say good-bye.

285
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:05,350
Oh, my God.

286
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:07,602
What did you say?

287
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:08,687
Nothing.

288
00:12:08,727 --> 00:12:10,146
What do you say
to that?

289
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:12,315
Ross, you've got to
tell her how you feel.

290
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:13,525
No way.

291
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,109
You can't just give up.

292
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,404
Is that what
a dinosaur would do?

293
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,447
What?

294
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:21,449
Dude, I'm just trying
to speak your language.

295
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:24,994
Ross, Rachel doesn't know

296
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:26,538
that you even want
to get back together.

297
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:28,331
If she did, she might
feel differently.

298
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:29,416
She might not even go.

299
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,792
You really think so?

300
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:32,919
I'm telling you.

301
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:33,961
Oh! Okay,

302
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,422
this is the part
of the musical

303
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:37,674
where there'd be
a really good,
convincing song.

304
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:39,259
♪ Bum-bum-bum-bum ♪

305
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:42,303
♪ Don't take no for an answer
bum-bum-bum ♪

306
00:12:42,345 --> 00:12:44,763
♪ Don't let love fly away,
bum-bum-bum-bum. ♪

307
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:46,182
Hi.

308
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:47,892
Can't a girl finish
a song around here?

309
00:12:47,934 --> 00:12:49,477
Hey.

310
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,769
Hi. So I just dropped
Emma off at my mom's.

311
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,021
Okay.

312
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:53,565
You're not taking her
with you tonight?

313
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:55,233
No, we decided
that I would go ahead

314
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:56,817
and set up first,

315
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,528
and then my mom would bring Emma
to Paris on Sunday.

316
00:12:58,570 --> 00:13:00,614
Wow, eight-hour flight
with a one-year-old.

317
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,198
Good luck, mom.

318
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,075
Eight hours with my mother
talking about Atkins?

319
00:13:04,117 --> 00:13:05,118
Good luck, Emma.

320
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:08,955
All right, you know what?
You're right.

321
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:10,665
I should at least
tell her how I feel.

322
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,293
Ross, wait, wait.

323
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,461
What? What?

324
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:16,254
Could you get me a muffin?

325
00:13:19,674 --> 00:13:21,175
Rachel?

326
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,885
Yeah?

327
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:25,138
I-I know you're
leaving tonight,

328
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:29,808
but I just have
to tell you...

329
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,851
I love you.

330
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:39,319
I don't know if that changes
your plans at all, but...

331
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,613
I thought you should know.

332
00:13:41,655 --> 00:13:45,116
Gunther...

333
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:49,663
Oh, I love you, too.

334
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:51,665
Probably not
in the same way,

335
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:53,333
but I do.

336
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:57,420
And when I'm in a cafe
having coffee,

337
00:13:57,462 --> 00:14:00,590
or I see a man with hair
brighter than the sun,

338
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:03,884
I'll think of you.

339
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,219
Oh.

340
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:10,266
Oh!

341
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:11,476
Bye, you guys.

342
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:12,811
Bye.

343
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:18,566
Oh, my God!

344
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:20,485
Unbelievable.

345
00:14:20,527 --> 00:14:22,320
Hey, you know
what might help?

346
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,238
I'm not getting you a muffin!

347
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:37,251
Do you think they recognize
each other from in there?

348
00:14:37,293 --> 00:14:39,212
Maybe.

349
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:40,963
Unless they're
like two people

350
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,465
who've lived
in apartments

351
00:14:42,507 --> 00:14:44,133
next to each other
for years

352
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:45,552
and then one day

353
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:47,721
they're pushed
through a vagina
and they meet.

354
00:14:47,762 --> 00:14:49,889
We're going to take Erica
to recovery now.

355
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:52,600
MONICA:
There's something
that we wanted to tell you.

356
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:58,105
We decided to name
the girl baby Erica.

357
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,107
Oh, my God.

358
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:01,609
That's just like my name!

359
00:15:03,862 --> 00:15:05,946
Son of a gun, it is.

360
00:15:07,741 --> 00:15:10,618
Anyway, I'm going
to go get some rest.

361
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:13,580
I'm really glad
I picked you guys.

362
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:16,499
You're going
to make great parents.

363
00:15:16,541 --> 00:15:18,543
Even Chandler.

364
00:15:20,712 --> 00:15:21,796
Okay, well bye.

365
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:22,839
Bye.

366
00:15:22,881 --> 00:15:23,840
We'll call you.

367
00:15:23,882 --> 00:15:24,841
Okay.

368
00:15:24,883 --> 00:15:26,801
Have fun at church camp.

369
00:15:32,432 --> 00:15:34,601
Oh, look at
these little buddies.

370
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:36,269
I know.

371
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,688
You ready to trade?

372
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,481
Okay.
Okay.

373
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:43,317
Oh, wait, let's see.

374
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:46,195
Take this little baby...

375
00:15:50,617 --> 00:15:52,076
Okay...

376
00:15:52,118 --> 00:15:53,912
We could trade later.

377
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,413
Yeah, I'm good.

378
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,627
Hey, what are you
working on?

379
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:02,962
Oh, it's a welcome-home sign
for the baby.

380
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:04,964
How sweet.

381
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:06,132
Oh, is that the baby?

382
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:09,343
No, I sat in the paint.

383
00:16:10,762 --> 00:16:11,721
Hey.

384
00:16:11,763 --> 00:16:13,389
So did you talk to Rachel?

385
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:16,142
No, and I'm not going to.

386
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:18,018
What?
Why not?

387
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:19,646
Because, she's just
going to shoot me down.

388
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:21,021
You guys saw what
happened with Gunther.

389
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,356
That did not look like fun.

390
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:25,067
How can you compare
yourself to Gunther?

391
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:27,695
I mean, sure, he's sexy
in a more obvious way.

392
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,991
But you have a relationship
with her.

393
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:33,701
You slept together last night.

394
00:16:33,743 --> 00:16:35,787
Yeah, and she still wants to go.

395
00:16:35,829 --> 00:16:37,747
It's pretty clear
where she is.

396
00:16:37,789 --> 00:16:40,124
Yeah, I know what you mean.
I mean, sometimes...

397
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:41,041
Uh, Joe.

398
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,209
Damn it!

399
00:16:44,295 --> 00:16:45,922
Look, even if I were
going to tell her,

400
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,465
I don't have to do it now.

401
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:48,842
Okay, I'll be seeing
her again; we've got time.

402
00:16:48,883 --> 00:16:50,217
No, you don't.

403
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,636
She's going to Paris.

404
00:16:51,678 --> 00:16:53,596
She is going
to meet somebody.

405
00:16:53,638 --> 00:16:56,098
Do you know how many hot guys
there are in Paris?

406
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,601
It's a city of Gunthers.

407
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,105
Hey.
PHOEBE:
Hey.

408
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,649
What do you have there?

409
00:17:04,691 --> 00:17:05,984
Oh, I made a little something.

410
00:17:06,024 --> 00:17:07,527
If I had more time
to work on it,

411
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:10,780
it'd be better, but...

412
00:17:10,822 --> 00:17:13,031
Oh, my God.
You did that yourself?

413
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:14,826
Honey, that's gorgeous.

414
00:17:14,868 --> 00:17:18,412
You know, the baby
can't read, Mike.

415
00:17:19,831 --> 00:17:22,166
Hi! You guys, the car service
just got here.

416
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:24,042
I can't believe
they're not home yet.

417
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:27,046
I have to catch my stupid plane.
I want to see the baby.

418
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,631
Monica just called
from the cab.

419
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:30,633
She said they
should be here
any minute.

420
00:17:30,675 --> 00:17:32,719
And apparently there's
some big surprise.

421
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,846
Yeah, but does she sound happy
about it?

422
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:36,890
Because my friend Ethel's baby
was born

423
00:17:36,931 --> 00:17:38,265
with a teeny-tiny beard.

424
00:17:41,352 --> 00:17:44,522
Oh!
Oh!
Oh, my God!

425
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:47,734
Hi.

426
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:48,985
Oh, my gosh.

427
00:17:49,027 --> 00:17:50,695
Hey.

428
00:17:50,737 --> 00:17:51,696
Hi.
Hey.

429
00:17:51,738 --> 00:17:53,489
( gasps )

430
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:57,076
Hey, so what
is the big surprise?

431
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:58,160
Oh!

432
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,749
( gasps )

433
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,500
Oh, my God.

434
00:18:04,542 --> 00:18:06,252
Okay, okay, okay,
awkward question:

435
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:08,212
The hospital knows
you took two, right?

436
00:18:08,254 --> 00:18:11,215
Yes. It's twins.

437
00:18:11,257 --> 00:18:12,926
Oh, they're so cute.

438
00:18:12,967 --> 00:18:14,719
Now, what kinds are they?

439
00:18:14,761 --> 00:18:18,598
This is a boy
and that's a girl.

440
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:19,933
Her name is Erica.

441
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:23,519
Hey, that pregnant girl's name
was Erica.

442
00:18:23,561 --> 00:18:24,979
Yeah. It's a shame

443
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:27,857
you two didn't get
to spend more
time together.

444
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:31,193
We named the boy Jack
after Dad.

445
00:18:31,235 --> 00:18:33,947
Oh, he's going
to be so happy.

446
00:18:33,988 --> 00:18:35,448
Jack Bing--
I love that.

447
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:37,742
Ooh, it sounds like
a '40s newspaper guy,

448
00:18:37,784 --> 00:18:40,244
you know, Jack Bing,
Morning Gazette.

449
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:42,789
"I'm going to blow
this story wide open."

450
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:47,085
Wow.

451
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,378
Oh, my gosh.

452
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:51,255
So beautiful.

453
00:18:51,297 --> 00:18:52,339
I want one.

454
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,340
Oh, yeah?

455
00:18:53,382 --> 00:18:54,634
Well, tell me which one,

456
00:18:54,675 --> 00:18:56,677
I'll try to slip it
in my coat.

457
00:18:58,054 --> 00:18:59,013
Seriously.

458
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:01,307
Want to make
one of those?

459
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,976
One? How about
a whole bunch?

460
00:19:03,017 --> 00:19:04,477
Really?
Yeah.

461
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,646
Oh, we can teach them
to sing

462
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:09,273
and we can be like
the von Trapp family.

463
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:10,650
Only without the Nazis.

464
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:12,401
Although, that sounds
kind of dull.

465
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:15,362
Oh, you guys.
I can't believe this.

466
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,490
If I don't leave now
I'm going to miss my plane.

467
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:19,533
I'm just so glad you
got to see the babies.

468
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:21,661
Me, too.

469
00:19:21,702 --> 00:19:24,330
I'm just sorry I'm not going
to be around

470
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:26,373
to watch you two attempt
to handle this.

471
00:19:28,126 --> 00:19:29,293
All right.

472
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:31,462
I can't say good-bye
to you guys again.

473
00:19:31,504 --> 00:19:34,256
I love you
all so much.

474
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:35,675
Love you.
Love you.

475
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:36,676
Call us
when you get there.

476
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:38,511
I will.

477
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,387
Ross, come here.

478
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:45,101
I just want you to know,

479
00:19:45,143 --> 00:19:48,146
last night...

480
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:53,026
I'll never forget it.

481
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:55,569
And neither will I.

482
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:05,621
All right, now I
really have to go.

483
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:06,747
Okay.

484
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:08,206
Au revoir.

485
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:09,667
Oh!

486
00:20:09,709 --> 00:20:14,213
They're going to really
hate me over there.

487
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,674
So you just let her go?

488
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,887
Yeah.

489
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,513
Hey, maybe that's
for the best.

490
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:23,597
Yeah?

491
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:24,849
Yeah.

492
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:27,185
You know, you just--
look, you got to...

493
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:30,688
you got to think about
last night the way she
does, okay?

494
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:32,272
You know, maybe...

495
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:35,902
maybe sleeping together
was the perfect way

496
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:37,277
to say good-bye.

497
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:39,321
Now she'll never
know how he feels.

498
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,281
But maybe that's okay,
you know?

499
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:44,035
Maybe...
Maybe it is better this way.

500
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:48,330
I mean, now...
now you can move on.

501
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:51,209
I mean, you've been
trying to for so long.

502
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:54,503
Maybe now that you're on
different continents...

503
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:56,714
Right?

504
00:21:00,009 --> 00:21:01,677
Maybe now you can
actually do it, you know?

505
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:03,262
You can...

506
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:07,808
You can
finally get over her.

507
00:21:11,104 --> 00:21:13,898
Yeah, that's true.

508
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:18,069
Except...

509
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:20,113
I don't want
to get over her.

510
00:21:20,154 --> 00:21:21,864
What?

511
00:21:21,906 --> 00:21:23,282
I don't.
I want to be with her.

512
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:24,366
Really?

513
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:25,367
Yeah, I'm going
to go after her.

514
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:26,744
Yeah, you are!

515
00:21:28,495 --> 00:21:29,914
PHOEBE:
Hey, wait.

516
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:31,373
Get your coat!
Get your coat!

517
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:32,499
My coat.

518
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:34,001
This is so cool!

519
00:21:34,043 --> 00:21:37,421
I have no idea
what's going on,
but I am excited!

520
00:21:37,463 --> 00:21:39,548
Ross, Ross!
What do you think
she's going to say?

521
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:40,883
I don't know.

522
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:42,342
But look, even
if she shoots me down,

523
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,220
at least I won't spend
the rest of my life

524
00:21:44,262 --> 00:21:45,930
wondering what
would have happened.

525
00:21:45,972 --> 00:21:47,056
Where is my coat?!

526
00:21:47,098 --> 00:21:49,308
You didn't bring one!

527
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:51,560
My cab's downstairs.
I'll drive you to the airport.

528
00:21:51,602 --> 00:21:52,770
Wish me luck.

529
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:54,105
Hurry!

530
00:21:54,147 --> 00:21:55,148
Good luck!

531
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:04,698
Okay.

532
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:06,242
There's no seat belt.

533
00:22:06,284 --> 00:22:07,743
That's okay.

534
00:22:07,785 --> 00:22:09,411
If we hit anything,
the engine will explode,

535
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:11,872
so, you know, it's better
if you're thrown from the car.

536
00:22:13,207 --> 00:22:14,500
All right, all right.
Let's do this.

537
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:15,709
Okay.

538
00:22:17,253 --> 00:22:18,254
Hey.

539
00:22:18,296 --> 00:22:19,421
80th and East End.

540
00:22:19,463 --> 00:22:20,965
No, I don't take passengers.

541
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:22,925
Hey, the law says
you have to accept any fare.

542
00:22:22,967 --> 00:22:25,178
No, you don't understand.
This isn't a real cab.

543
00:22:25,219 --> 00:22:27,263
I'm going to report you.
What's your medallion number?

544
00:22:27,305 --> 00:22:29,807
My medallion number is
"Get out of the cab!"

545
00:22:29,849 --> 00:22:30,808
What?

546
00:22:30,850 --> 00:22:32,643
Get out of the cab!

547
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:34,312
Get out of the cab!

548
00:22:34,352 --> 00:22:35,604
( yelling )

549
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,276
Oh, hey, hey.

550
00:22:40,318 --> 00:22:42,360
Can I give you guys
your housewarming present now?

551
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:43,612
Now that you can do.

552
00:22:43,654 --> 00:22:45,363
All right.

553
00:22:50,911 --> 00:22:53,998
Ah...

554
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:55,958
Chick, Jr.?

555
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,502
Duck, Jr...

556
00:22:59,879 --> 00:23:02,131
Don't hide from Mama!

557
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:10,931
( groans )

558
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:12,432
You can open your eyes now.

559
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:13,809
Are we off the bridge?

560
00:23:13,851 --> 00:23:15,228
Yes.

561
00:23:15,269 --> 00:23:17,563
Is the old woman on the bicycle
still alive?

562
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:20,774
Yeah, she jumped right back up.

563
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:23,194
Oh, my God.
Phoebe, slow down!

564
00:23:23,236 --> 00:23:25,196
Do you want to get
to Rachel in time?

565
00:23:25,238 --> 00:23:27,531
Yes, but I don't want to die
in your cab.

566
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:30,076
You should have thought of that
before you got in.

567
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:32,578
Toll booth.

568
00:23:32,619 --> 00:23:34,288
What?
Toll booth!

569
00:23:35,873 --> 00:23:37,333
Four bucks.

570
00:23:37,375 --> 00:23:38,751
There are quarters
in the glove compartment.

571
00:23:40,878 --> 00:23:42,671
Hurry!
( startled yell )

572
00:23:43,881 --> 00:23:44,882
Okay.

573
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:46,675
( yells )

574
00:23:46,717 --> 00:23:49,095
Damn, that window's clean.

575
00:23:50,263 --> 00:23:51,597
Quack, quack.
Tweet, tweet.

576
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:52,639
Quack, quack.

577
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:53,724
Tweet, tweet.

578
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:55,475
Quack, quack.

579
00:23:55,517 --> 00:23:57,228
Tweet, tweet.
Quack, quack.

580
00:23:57,270 --> 00:24:01,065
Tweet, tweet.
Quack, tweet, quack.

581
00:24:01,107 --> 00:24:03,609
We were wondering what was
taking so long with the gift,

582
00:24:03,650 --> 00:24:07,071
but now we understand
you were doing this.

583
00:24:09,073 --> 00:24:12,243
Okay, I wanted
to surprise you, but...

584
00:24:12,285 --> 00:24:13,911
for your housewarming gift,

585
00:24:13,953 --> 00:24:16,789
I got you a baby chick
and a baby duck.

586
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:19,917
Really?
You got us a chick and a duck?

587
00:24:19,959 --> 00:24:21,668
Oh, great.

588
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,212
Just what you want
for a new house
with infants--

589
00:24:23,254 --> 00:24:25,965
bird feces.

590
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:27,549
But they must have
jumped off the table,

591
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:28,717
'cause now they're gone.

592
00:24:28,759 --> 00:24:30,219
Don't worry,
we'll find them.

593
00:24:30,261 --> 00:24:32,430
Actually, I'm going to
go check on the twins.

594
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:33,513
Oh, God!

595
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:35,724
What did I just step on?

596
00:24:35,766 --> 00:24:37,475
It's okay, it's
just an egg roll.

597
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:38,811
Oh.

598
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:42,231
You stepped on my egg roll?!

599
00:24:42,273 --> 00:24:43,899
I'm sorry.

600
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:45,609
I didn't know to look for
Chinese food on the floor.

601
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:47,445
Just put it on
a plate and leave.

602
00:24:51,573 --> 00:24:53,575
Okay.
Let's find these birds.

603
00:24:53,617 --> 00:24:55,161
All right.

604
00:24:57,788 --> 00:24:58,747
( chirping )

605
00:24:58,789 --> 00:25:00,958
Wait, you hear that?

606
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,418
( chirping )

607
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:03,461
( gasps )

608
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:05,671
They're in the table!

609
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:07,631
Well, that can't be good.

610
00:25:07,673 --> 00:25:09,925
We've got to get them
out of there.
How?

611
00:25:09,967 --> 00:25:11,593
Oh. Oh.
Maybe we can lure them out.

612
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:12,886
You know any bird calls?

613
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:15,639
Oh, tons.
I'm quite the woodsman.

614
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:18,017
Well, uh...

615
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:20,144
maybe we can just
tip the table a little.

616
00:25:20,186 --> 00:25:22,313
Joey, wait!
The ball!
Oh!

617
00:25:22,355 --> 00:25:25,816
( ball clanging )

618
00:25:27,485 --> 00:25:30,904
( clanks )

619
00:25:34,367 --> 00:25:35,451
( chirping )

620
00:25:35,493 --> 00:25:38,871
Oh, God!
( sighs )

621
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:40,580
So what do we do?

622
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:42,791
I don't know, maybe we
can open this up somehow.

623
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:44,835
Okay.

624
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:47,296
No.

625
00:25:47,338 --> 00:25:49,256
It's all glued together.

626
00:25:49,298 --> 00:25:52,468
That mean
we have to bust it open?

627
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:55,095
I don't know, maybe.

628
00:25:55,137 --> 00:25:56,472
Oh, my God.

629
00:25:56,514 --> 00:25:57,473
I know, it's...

630
00:25:57,515 --> 00:26:02,144
it's the foosball table.

631
00:26:02,186 --> 00:26:05,563
All right, you know what?
We don't have a choice.

632
00:26:05,605 --> 00:26:07,441
It's like I would have said
in that sci-fi movie

633
00:26:07,483 --> 00:26:08,901
if had gotten the part...

634
00:26:10,652 --> 00:26:14,073
Those are our men in there.
We have to get them out.

635
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:16,158
Even if I have to sacrifice

636
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:18,369
the most important thing
in my life--

637
00:26:18,411 --> 00:26:20,413
my time machine.

638
00:26:20,454 --> 00:26:23,374
Did that movie ever get made?

639
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:24,875
It did not.

640
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:33,259
Ross, where you going?

641
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,843
To talk to Rachel.

642
00:26:34,885 --> 00:26:37,221
Isn't that why we took a ride
in the death cab?

643
00:26:37,263 --> 00:26:39,557
What are you gonna do,
just walk up to her at the gate?

644
00:26:39,597 --> 00:26:42,017
Have you never chased anyone
through the airport before?

645
00:26:42,059 --> 00:26:44,520
Not since my cop show
got canceled.

646
00:26:44,562 --> 00:26:48,065
You have to get a ticket
to get past security.

647
00:26:48,107 --> 00:26:49,483
What?
We're never gonna make it.

648
00:26:49,525 --> 00:26:52,236
Not with that attitude.
Now haul ass.

649
00:26:54,447 --> 00:26:58,284
Okay, if you could all walk
slower that'd be great.

650
00:27:05,291 --> 00:27:07,793
Madame.
Your passport, please?

651
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:09,169
Oh, my God.

652
00:27:09,211 --> 00:27:10,837
I was so afraid
I wasn't going to remember

653
00:27:10,879 --> 00:27:12,298
any of my high school French,

654
00:27:12,339 --> 00:27:14,841
but I understood
every word you just said.

655
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:17,094
Your boarding pass, please?

656
00:27:17,136 --> 00:27:17,928
Oh.

657
00:27:19,513 --> 00:27:20,931
Oh.

658
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:23,309
Shoot, I had it.

659
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:24,642
Oh, I can't believe this.

660
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:26,353
Madame, if you don't have...

661
00:27:26,395 --> 00:27:27,813
I have it, I have it!
I have it!

662
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:30,232
Oh.

663
00:27:30,274 --> 00:27:31,609
Okay, I can't find it.

664
00:27:31,649 --> 00:27:35,195
But I remember
that I was in seat 32C...

665
00:27:35,237 --> 00:27:38,157
because that's my bra size.

666
00:27:38,198 --> 00:27:40,742
Madame, you must have
your boarding pass.

667
00:27:40,784 --> 00:27:42,328
Okay, fine.
But you know what?

668
00:27:42,369 --> 00:27:44,371
If I was in 36D we would not
be having this problem.

669
00:27:51,837 --> 00:27:53,464
Hi, I need a ticket.

670
00:27:53,506 --> 00:27:54,756
Just one?

671
00:27:54,798 --> 00:27:56,091
I drive you all
the way down here,

672
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:57,675
I don't get to see
how it works out?

673
00:27:57,717 --> 00:28:00,095
Fine, two tickets.
I need two tickets.

674
00:28:00,137 --> 00:28:03,098
We're on our honeymoon.

675
00:28:03,140 --> 00:28:04,975
And the destination?

676
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:06,977
I don't care,
whatever's the cheapest.

677
00:28:07,019 --> 00:28:09,480
I'm so lucky
I married you.

678
00:28:11,607 --> 00:28:13,317
Oh, shoot!

679
00:28:13,359 --> 00:28:15,986
Damn it.
Where is it?

680
00:28:16,028 --> 00:28:17,988
Oh, oh. I found it!
I found it!

681
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:19,448
Ha! Ha! I found it!

682
00:28:19,490 --> 00:28:21,325
I told you I would find it.
In your face!

683
00:28:21,367 --> 00:28:22,493
You're a different person.

684
00:28:26,246 --> 00:28:30,543
Okay.
Flight 421 to Paris.

685
00:28:30,584 --> 00:28:31,751
I don't see it.

686
00:28:31,793 --> 00:28:33,462
Do you see it?
No, did we miss it?

687
00:28:33,504 --> 00:28:34,712
No, no, no.
It's impossible.

688
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,840
It doesn't leave
for another 20 minutes.

689
00:28:36,882 --> 00:28:38,884
Well, we have the
flight number wrong.

690
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,847
( phone rings )

691
00:28:43,889 --> 00:28:44,973
Hello?

692
00:28:45,015 --> 00:28:48,185
Hey, it's me.
Here's Ross.

693
00:28:48,227 --> 00:28:49,769
Hey.
Hey, listen...

694
00:28:49,811 --> 00:28:51,313
Oh, my God.
Ross, you wouldn't believe

695
00:28:51,355 --> 00:28:53,148
the cute little noises
the twins are making.

696
00:28:53,190 --> 00:28:54,191
Listen.

697
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:56,402
Monica...

698
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:57,903
Monica.

699
00:28:57,944 --> 00:28:59,737
Monica. Monica.

700
00:28:59,779 --> 00:29:01,156
Monica.

701
00:29:01,198 --> 00:29:02,700
Oh, I'm sorry.

702
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:04,034
Shoot, they were
doing it before.

703
00:29:04,076 --> 00:29:05,285
That's all right.
Listen, listen...

704
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:06,412
Wait, wait.
Here they go again.

705
00:29:07,621 --> 00:29:09,540
Monica. Monica.

706
00:29:09,582 --> 00:29:11,625
Monica. Monica.

707
00:29:11,667 --> 00:29:13,544
Monica?
Isn't that cute?

708
00:29:13,586 --> 00:29:15,003
That was precious!
Listen.

709
00:29:16,714 --> 00:29:19,007
I need Rachel's
flight information.

710
00:29:19,049 --> 00:29:20,426
Oh, okay.

711
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:24,221
All right, it's Flight 421.
Leaves at 8:40.

712
00:29:24,263 --> 00:29:26,557
Yes, that's what I have.
It's not on the board.

713
00:29:26,599 --> 00:29:28,934
That's what it says here.
Flight 421 leaves at 8:40.

714
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:30,436
Newark Airport.

715
00:29:30,477 --> 00:29:31,437
What?

716
00:29:31,478 --> 00:29:32,938
Newark Airport.

717
00:29:32,979 --> 00:29:34,814
Why, where are you?

718
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:37,610
JFK.

719
00:30:06,388 --> 00:30:07,765
( shouting ):
Don't worry, you guys!

720
00:30:07,805 --> 00:30:09,767
We're going to get you
out of there!

721
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:14,480
And we're also going
to buy you tiny bird
hearing aids.

722
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:21,737
Okay...

723
00:30:21,779 --> 00:30:23,196
here goes.

724
00:30:27,618 --> 00:30:29,077
What's the matter?

725
00:30:29,119 --> 00:30:33,999
I need to say good-bye
to the table first.

726
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:36,834
I understand.

727
00:30:37,961 --> 00:30:40,589
Okay...

728
00:30:40,631 --> 00:30:43,133
( sighs )

729
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:45,761
Table...

730
00:30:45,803 --> 00:30:51,099
you have given us
so many great times.

731
00:30:51,141 --> 00:30:53,310
And you guys,

732
00:30:53,352 --> 00:31:00,317
Jordan, Victor, Joel,
all of you guys...

733
00:31:00,359 --> 00:31:01,610
what can I say?

734
00:31:01,652 --> 00:31:10,536
You guys make us look good.

735
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:12,870
You want to say anything?

736
00:31:12,912 --> 00:31:15,457
I don't know.

737
00:31:15,499 --> 00:31:16,583
( sighs )

738
00:31:16,625 --> 00:31:21,129
Except that,
for one last time...

739
00:31:21,171 --> 00:31:22,506
Good game.
Good game.

740
00:31:22,548 --> 00:31:23,841
Good game. Good game.

741
00:31:23,881 --> 00:31:25,509
Good game. Good game.
Good game.

742
00:31:25,551 --> 00:31:27,803
Yeah, yeah.

743
00:31:27,845 --> 00:31:29,304
Good game.

744
00:31:32,725 --> 00:31:34,727
Okay, here we go.

745
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:44,570
I can't do it.

746
00:31:45,738 --> 00:31:47,573
Well, I can't
do it, either.

747
00:31:49,199 --> 00:31:50,367
Hey, did you find them?

748
00:31:50,409 --> 00:31:51,827
Yeah, they're stuck
inside the table.

749
00:31:51,869 --> 00:31:53,245
Yeah, and we have
to bust it open,

750
00:31:53,286 --> 00:31:55,497
but neither of us can do it.

751
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:56,998
Aw... well, sure.

752
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,667
It's got to be so hard.

753
00:32:00,043 --> 00:32:01,378
I'll do it. Give me!

754
00:32:06,383 --> 00:32:07,843
ROSS:
Phoebe!

755
00:32:07,885 --> 00:32:08,844
PHOEBE:
Whoa!

756
00:32:08,886 --> 00:32:09,969
No, no, no, no, no!

757
00:32:10,011 --> 00:32:12,222
( high pitched squeals )

758
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:15,141
I've never gone
this fast before.

759
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:16,935
Phoebe, forget it.
Okay?

760
00:32:16,976 --> 00:32:18,645
Newark is like, an hour away.

761
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:20,647
There's no way we're going
to make it in time.

762
00:32:20,689 --> 00:32:22,691
She's got her cell.
You could call her.

763
00:32:22,733 --> 00:32:24,651
I am not doing this
over the phone.

764
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:26,695
You don't have any other choice.

765
00:32:26,737 --> 00:32:28,238
( screams )

766
00:32:30,783 --> 00:32:33,159
( cell phone rings )

767
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:34,536
Hello?

768
00:32:34,578 --> 00:32:36,121
Rachel.
Oh, good!

769
00:32:36,162 --> 00:32:38,206
Hey, by the way, did you just
get on the plane?

770
00:32:38,248 --> 00:32:40,166
Yeah.
For what it's worth,
we would've caught her

771
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:41,501
if we were at
the right airport.

772
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:44,337
Yay.

773
00:32:44,379 --> 00:32:46,965
Rach, hang on.

774
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:48,842
( mouthing words )

775
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:50,761
Phoebe, is everything okay?

776
00:32:51,929 --> 00:32:55,014
Um... actually, no.

777
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:57,893
No, you have to
get off the plane.

778
00:32:57,935 --> 00:32:59,478
What? Why?

779
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:01,438
I have this feeling
that something's wrong with it.

780
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:05,818
Something is wrong with
the left, filangee.

781
00:33:07,611 --> 00:33:10,656
Oh, honey, I'm sure there's
nothing wrong with the plane.

782
00:33:10,697 --> 00:33:11,990
All right, look,
I have to go.

783
00:33:12,031 --> 00:33:13,492
I love you,
and I will call you

784
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:15,285
the minute I get to Paris.

785
00:33:17,287 --> 00:33:20,165
Um... what was that?

786
00:33:20,206 --> 00:33:21,917
Oh, that was just
my crazy friend.

787
00:33:21,959 --> 00:33:23,669
She told me I should
get off the plane

788
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:26,672
because she had a feeling
that there was something wrong

789
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:29,466
with the left filangee.

790
00:33:29,508 --> 00:33:32,469
Okay, that doesn't
sound good.

791
00:33:32,511 --> 00:33:33,804
I wouldn't worry about it.

792
00:33:33,846 --> 00:33:35,180
She's always coming up
with stuff like this.

793
00:33:35,221 --> 00:33:36,849
And you know what,
she's almost never right.

794
00:33:36,890 --> 00:33:38,266
But she is sometimes?

795
00:33:38,308 --> 00:33:39,685
Well...?

796
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:43,271
What are you doing?

797
00:33:43,313 --> 00:33:44,564
Well, I can't
take this plane now.

798
00:33:44,606 --> 00:33:46,065
Excuse me, sir?
Where you going?

799
00:33:46,107 --> 00:33:47,609
I have to get off
this plane, okay?

800
00:33:47,651 --> 00:33:49,945
Her friend has a feeling

801
00:33:49,987 --> 00:33:51,989
something's wrong
with the left filangee.

802
00:33:56,284 --> 00:33:58,035
Could I get some peanuts?

803
00:33:59,538 --> 00:34:00,706
What's wrong with the plane?

804
00:34:00,747 --> 00:34:02,332
There's nothing wrong
with the plane.

805
00:34:02,374 --> 00:34:03,750
The left filangee.

806
00:34:03,792 --> 00:34:05,627
There's no filangee.

807
00:34:05,669 --> 00:34:06,962
Oh, my God.

808
00:34:07,004 --> 00:34:08,547
This plane doesn't even
have a filangee.

809
00:34:09,923 --> 00:34:11,216
Well, then I'm not
flying on it.

810
00:34:11,257 --> 00:34:12,175
Ma'am, please sit down.

811
00:34:12,217 --> 00:34:13,176
What's going on?

812
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:14,344
We're all getting off.

813
00:34:14,386 --> 00:34:15,721
There is no filangee!

814
00:34:20,225 --> 00:34:22,895
This is ridiculous. I...

815
00:34:24,730 --> 00:34:26,063
Yeah, okay.

816
00:34:29,776 --> 00:34:32,905
( chirping )

817
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:36,366
( sighing ):
All right.

818
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:38,827
My job here is done.

819
00:34:38,869 --> 00:34:42,247
That was... impressive.

820
00:34:42,288 --> 00:34:45,500
Y-Yeah. You didn't even use
the tools for most of it.

821
00:34:46,835 --> 00:34:48,837
Eh, they were just
slowing me down.

822
00:34:48,879 --> 00:34:51,548
All right, I got to
get back to the babies.

823
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:53,884
See you girls later.

824
00:34:57,262 --> 00:34:59,514
Sorry about the table, man.

825
00:34:59,556 --> 00:35:00,766
Yeah.

826
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:03,142
You going to buy a new one?

827
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:05,186
Probably not.

828
00:35:05,228 --> 00:35:07,064
No.

829
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:10,734
I don't know how much I'm going
to want to play after you go.

830
00:35:12,945 --> 00:35:15,363
Well, at least we got
these little guys out.

831
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:16,740
Yeah.

832
00:35:16,782 --> 00:35:19,116
Oh! We were worried
about you.

833
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:23,162
Hmm.

834
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:26,666
Guess I better get used to
things crapping in my hand, huh?

835
00:35:36,051 --> 00:35:38,553
Oh, I'm going to miss
these little guys.

836
00:35:38,595 --> 00:35:40,931
It was nice
having birds around again.

837
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:44,142
Hey, you know what?

838
00:35:44,183 --> 00:35:46,478
Maybe we should keep
them here with you.

839
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:48,229
What?

840
00:35:48,271 --> 00:35:50,732
Yeah. I mean, we've got
a lot going on right now.

841
00:35:50,774 --> 00:35:52,943
And plus, here, they'd
have their own room.

842
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:56,446
I could get a goose!

843
00:35:57,823 --> 00:36:01,701
You know, I think you're
set with the poultry.

844
00:36:03,328 --> 00:36:04,871
Thanks, man.

845
00:36:04,913 --> 00:36:06,123
You hear that, you guys?

846
00:36:06,163 --> 00:36:07,791
You're going to get
to stay here.

847
00:36:07,833 --> 00:36:10,669
And-and it's good, you know?

848
00:36:10,710 --> 00:36:13,421
'Cause, uh...

849
00:36:13,463 --> 00:36:16,299
'cause now you have
a reason to come visit.

850
00:36:18,844 --> 00:36:22,555
I think there may be
another reason.

851
00:36:29,688 --> 00:36:31,648
So, uh...

852
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:38,488
awkward hug or lame,
cool-guy handshake.

853
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:40,866
( clears throat ):
Yeah, well, you know,

854
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:42,450
lame, cool-guy handshake.

855
00:36:43,952 --> 00:36:47,164
Doo-doo-doo-doo!
Doo-doo-doo-doo!

856
00:37:01,053 --> 00:37:03,805
Ma'am I assure you,
the plane is fine.

857
00:37:03,847 --> 00:37:06,850
And you fixed the filangee?

858
00:37:06,892 --> 00:37:08,810
Yes, the filangee is fixed.

859
00:37:08,852 --> 00:37:11,604
As a matter of fact,
we put a whole lot

860
00:37:11,646 --> 00:37:14,607
of extra filangees on board,
just in case.

861
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,238
Where is she?

862
00:37:20,279 --> 00:37:21,531
I don't see her.

863
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:23,491
Rachel!
Rachel Greene!
There she is!

864
00:37:23,533 --> 00:37:25,326
Rachel! Rachel!

865
00:37:25,368 --> 00:37:27,495
Whoa, whoa, excuse me, sir.
Do you have a boarding pass?

866
00:37:27,537 --> 00:37:28,997
No, no, I just
have to talk to someone

867
00:37:29,039 --> 00:37:30,707
that's getting on
the plane.
I'm sorry, sir.

868
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:32,667
You cannot go any further
without a boarding pass.

869
00:37:32,709 --> 00:37:34,086
No, no, no. But I...

870
00:37:34,127 --> 00:37:37,505
You don't understand...
Rachel!

871
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:39,257
What?

872
00:37:39,298 --> 00:37:41,593
Oh, my God. What are you...?
What are you guys doing here?

873
00:37:41,634 --> 00:37:44,470
Okay. You're on.

874
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:46,556
What? What, Ross?
Okay, you're scaring me.

875
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:47,849
What's going on?

876
00:37:47,891 --> 00:37:48,934
Okay.

877
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:50,018
The thing is...

878
00:37:50,060 --> 00:37:51,019
Yeah?

879
00:37:51,061 --> 00:37:53,105
Don't go.

880
00:37:53,146 --> 00:37:54,272
What?

881
00:37:54,313 --> 00:37:55,941
Please, please
stay with me.

882
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:57,943
I am so in love with you.

883
00:37:57,984 --> 00:37:59,236
Please don't go.

884
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,445
Oh, my God.

885
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:02,155
I know. I know.

886
00:38:02,197 --> 00:38:04,824
I shouldn't have waited
till now to say it,

887
00:38:04,866 --> 00:38:06,868
but, um... that
was stupid, okay?

888
00:38:06,910 --> 00:38:09,037
I'm sorry, but
I'm telling you now.

889
00:38:09,079 --> 00:38:10,538
I love you.

890
00:38:10,580 --> 00:38:14,167
Do not get on this plane.

891
00:38:14,209 --> 00:38:15,460
Miss?
I...

892
00:38:15,501 --> 00:38:16,878
Are you boarding
the plane?

893
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:18,713
Hey, hey.

894
00:38:18,755 --> 00:38:21,049
I know you love me.

895
00:38:21,091 --> 00:38:23,843
I know you do.

896
00:38:23,885 --> 00:38:25,303
Miss?

897
00:38:25,344 --> 00:38:26,554
I... I...

898
00:38:26,596 --> 00:38:28,556
I have to get on the plane.

899
00:38:28,598 --> 00:38:29,557
No, you don't.

900
00:38:29,599 --> 00:38:30,976
Yes, I do.
No, you don't.

901
00:38:31,017 --> 00:38:32,560
I do. They're waiting
for me, Ross.

902
00:38:32,602 --> 00:38:34,312
I can't do this right now.

903
00:38:34,353 --> 00:38:36,856
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry.

904
00:38:36,898 --> 00:38:38,942
Rachel?

905
00:38:38,984 --> 00:38:40,860
( half-whispers ):
I'm so sorry.

906
00:38:55,792 --> 00:38:57,961
I really thought she'd stay.

907
00:38:58,003 --> 00:38:59,712
I know.

908
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:01,047
I'm sorry.

909
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:05,760
Oh!

910
00:39:09,306 --> 00:39:11,390
( sobs )

911
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:16,188
Well...

912
00:39:16,229 --> 00:39:18,439
that's it.

913
00:39:18,481 --> 00:39:20,483
Everything's packed.

914
00:39:21,734 --> 00:39:23,987
Wow.

915
00:39:24,029 --> 00:39:25,613
This is weird.

916
00:39:25,655 --> 00:39:26,865
I know.

917
00:39:26,906 --> 00:39:28,283
Yeah.

918
00:39:28,325 --> 00:39:31,744
Uh, does this mean
there's nothing to eat?

919
00:39:33,454 --> 00:39:35,456
I put three lasagnas
in your freezer.

920
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,375
I love you.

921
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,089
Hey.
Hey.

922
00:39:43,131 --> 00:39:44,757
Hey, so, did you guys
make it in time?

923
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:46,634
Yeah, yeah.
He talked to her.

924
00:39:46,676 --> 00:39:49,221
But, um, she got
on the plane, anyway.

925
00:39:51,181 --> 00:39:53,099
Where's Ross?

926
00:39:53,141 --> 00:39:55,476
He went home.
He didn't want to see anybody.

927
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:57,645
Oh.

928
00:40:10,867 --> 00:40:12,952
( beeps )

929
00:40:12,994 --> 00:40:15,372
RACHEL:
Ross, hi.

930
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,082
It's me.

931
00:40:17,123 --> 00:40:22,170
I just got back on the plane,
and I just feel awful.

932
00:40:22,212 --> 00:40:26,883
That is so not how I wanted
things to end with us.

933
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:30,678
It's... it's just that I...
wasn't expecting to see you,

934
00:40:30,720 --> 00:40:33,139
and then all of a sudden
you're there

935
00:40:33,181 --> 00:40:34,807
and saying these things.

936
00:40:34,849 --> 00:40:38,853
And... now I'm just sitting here
and thinking

937
00:40:38,895 --> 00:40:43,358
of all the stuff I should have
said and I didn't.

938
00:40:43,400 --> 00:40:47,695
I mean, I didn't even get to
tell you that I love you, too.

939
00:40:47,737 --> 00:40:51,366
Because of course I do.
I love you.

940
00:40:53,326 --> 00:40:54,911
I love you.

941
00:40:56,079 --> 00:40:58,206
I love you.

942
00:40:58,248 --> 00:41:00,292
What am I doing?

943
00:41:00,333 --> 00:41:03,128
I love you.

944
00:41:03,169 --> 00:41:05,546
( sighs ):
I've got to see you.

945
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:08,091
I've got to get off this plane.

946
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:10,009
Oh, my God.

947
00:41:10,051 --> 00:41:11,386
RACHEL:
Okay, ex-excuse me.

948
00:41:11,428 --> 00:41:12,804
WOMAN:
Miss, please,
sit down!

949
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:14,847
No, I'm sorry,
I'm really sorry.

950
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:16,391
But I need to get
off the plane, okay?

951
00:41:16,433 --> 00:41:17,976
I need to just tell someone
that I love them.

952
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:19,394
Miss, I can't let you
off the plane.

953
00:41:19,436 --> 00:41:23,356
Let her off the plane!

954
00:41:23,398 --> 00:41:25,984
I am afraid you are going
to have to take your seat.

955
00:41:26,025 --> 00:41:27,944
Oh, please.
Miss, you don't
understand.

956
00:41:27,986 --> 00:41:30,738
Try to understand!

957
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:32,407
Oh, come on, Miss.
Isn't there any way

958
00:41:32,449 --> 00:41:33,992
that you can just
let me off the...?

959
00:41:34,033 --> 00:41:34,993
( beeps )

960
00:41:35,034 --> 00:41:37,120
No, no!

961
00:41:37,162 --> 00:41:39,998
Oh, my God.
Did she get off the plane?

962
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:42,125
Did she get off the plane?

963
00:41:43,500 --> 00:41:46,754
I got off the plane.

964
00:41:55,138 --> 00:41:58,266
You got off the plane.

965
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:11,446
I do love you.

966
00:42:11,488 --> 00:42:13,114
Oh!

967
00:42:13,156 --> 00:42:16,075
I love you, too, and I am
never letting you go again.

968
00:42:16,117 --> 00:42:18,244
Okay, 'cause this
is where I want to be.

969
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:19,787
Okay? No more messing around.

970
00:42:19,829 --> 00:42:21,580
I don't want to
mess this up again.

971
00:42:21,622 --> 00:42:23,749
Me, neither. Okay? We are...
we're done being stupid.

972
00:42:23,791 --> 00:42:24,959
Okay.

973
00:42:25,001 --> 00:42:26,461
It's you and me,
all right? This is it.

974
00:42:26,503 --> 00:42:27,628
This is it.

975
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:30,840
Unless we're on a break.

976
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:41,851
Don't make jokes now.

977
00:43:02,914 --> 00:43:04,332
Okay, please be careful
with that.

978
00:43:04,374 --> 00:43:05,917
It was my grandmother's.
Be careful.

979
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:08,002
Thank you.

980
00:43:08,044 --> 00:43:11,381
Uh, if that falls off
the truck, it wouldn't
be the worst thing.

981
00:43:19,472 --> 00:43:21,598
Wow.

982
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:24,769
I know.

983
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:26,687
It seems smaller somehow.

984
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:28,314
Hmm.

985
00:43:28,356 --> 00:43:32,068
Has it always been purple?

986
00:43:35,029 --> 00:43:37,198
Look around, you guys.

987
00:43:37,240 --> 00:43:39,451
This was your first home.

988
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:43,538
And it was a happy place--

989
00:43:43,580 --> 00:43:46,707
filled with love and laughter,

990
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:49,043
but more important,
because of rent control,

991
00:43:49,085 --> 00:43:51,379
it was a friggin' steal.

992
00:43:56,092 --> 00:43:58,844
Hey, do you realize
that at one time or another,

993
00:43:58,886 --> 00:44:00,638
we all lived
in this apartment?

994
00:44:00,679 --> 00:44:02,932
Oh, yeah, that's true.

995
00:44:02,974 --> 00:44:05,268
Uh, I haven't.

996
00:44:05,310 --> 00:44:06,685
Wait a minute.

997
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:08,146
What about
that summer

998
00:44:08,187 --> 00:44:10,231
during college that you
lived with Grandma

999
00:44:10,273 --> 00:44:12,233
and you tried to
make it as a dancer?

1000
00:44:17,654 --> 00:44:20,074
Do you realize we
almost made it ten years

1001
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:21,576
without that coming up?

1002
00:44:25,830 --> 00:44:27,290
Oh, honey,
I forgot.

1003
00:44:27,332 --> 00:44:29,250
I promised Treeger
that we'd leave our keys.

1004
00:44:29,292 --> 00:44:30,376
Oh, okay.

1005
00:45:03,993 --> 00:45:05,286
( sighs )

1006
00:45:05,328 --> 00:45:06,954
So, I guess this is it.

1007
00:45:06,996 --> 00:45:09,790
Yeah.

1008
00:45:09,832 --> 00:45:11,668
I guess so.

1009
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:14,920
( voice breaking ):
This is harder

1010
00:45:14,962 --> 00:45:16,381
than I thought
it would be.

1011
00:45:16,422 --> 00:45:18,591
Oh, it's going to be okay.

1012
00:45:21,344 --> 00:45:23,304
Okay.

1013
00:45:28,518 --> 00:45:30,353
( sniffling )

1014
00:45:30,395 --> 00:45:32,729
Do you guys have to go
to the new house right away,

1015
00:45:32,771 --> 00:45:34,691
or do you have some time?

1016
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:38,695
We got some time.

1017
00:45:38,735 --> 00:45:40,988
Okay, should we get
some coffee?

1018
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:42,907
Sure.

1019
00:45:42,948 --> 00:45:44,283
Okay.

1020
00:45:44,325 --> 00:45:45,951
Where?

1021
00:45:53,918 --> 00:45:56,379
( half-whispers ):
Oh, thanks, guys.

1022
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:10,851
Captioned by
